re the celestials. in the presence of all the Rşis and gods, the Sun and Moon announced the innocence of the daughter of Janaka.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-45-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7044006","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c62c4474a6e09a4f43492c55d54e1beb67e2c8180cab31c65c57ab2bbb7b9a93","compact":"a45a78a61dbf4b28dc05c8a4212e3aea68f3bcacdc5293cb8573cc28e9800da8","nasal":"a45a78a61dbf4b28dc05c8a4212e3aea68f3bcacdc5293cb8573cc28e9800da8"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-44-7","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":44,"verse":7,"english":"To secure my confidence, Sītā, in your very presence, entered fire. At that time, O Saumitri, fire, carrying sacrificial oblations and the wind of the sky declared Sītā's innocence before the celestials. in the presence of all the Rşis and gods, the Sun and Moon announced the innocence of the daughter of Janaka. Indra, the king of the celestials, himself handed over the chaste Sītā to me in the island of Lanka.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.476,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-45-6","DUTT-7-45-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7044007","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"281c648be784a5691a303ae9302e429e4ef8017fce0622292be2e998e248c1a6","compact":"40a84c4675ee137af2e59e1ea172557083c1cfe36513fd3385b48220f17879be","nasal":"3191f9eba1d32abebc25c727674807997423f134164115e51bff335e28a36296"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-44-8","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":44,"verse":8,"english":"Indra, the king of the celestials, himself handed over the chaste Sītā to me in the island of Lanka.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.933,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-45-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7044008","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"dd283e54f25de553c929235db48636f0356eb3257eb8c084a85adaad95c54a2e","compact":"0a0bcfc796e66b7950a46eb2250e0b2772ca612454bb8ce28d3b437949de77c1","nasal":"149c0fd552e3ba508c4392ade4bfe80956014f1c61c9c83d2957dec2b37a6430"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-44-9","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":44,"verse":9,"english":"My mind know Sītā as chaste for ever. So, at that time, I came back to Ayodhya with Sita.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-45-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7044009","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3a6549dd90f6e980d2a2a9dc7973e0077b5a8a2efae7f2013d2c2edec401d2bc","compact":"d1d85e7bbb6fff3722c5c9f97c7ddf533f30283eab2d258cbc73b171fa48912c","nasal":"bb5c2288f91105f3bf5451a30e6b21edf086e8badcdc6dfd366a23a8ef4c6dd8"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-44-10","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":44,"verse":10,"english":"But now a great sorrow consequent upon the censure of the citizens and villagers has pierced my heart.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-45-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7044010","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"77391d0ab5ee004fa5e7babdcefa5c121a327289dd75b5b4892a1abb7babdc5f","compact":"c5d1810e6a4a91f9a4a51227afcd6dee41744b03a7cf4425d1f63e0b2d2ea752","nasal":"c5d1810e6a4a91f9a4a51227afcd6dee41744b03a7cf4425d1f63e0b2d2ea752"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-44-11","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":44,"verse":11,"english":"He, who is notorious on this earth and as long as that notoriety remains current, is classed among the vile.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.768,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-45-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7044011","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ec188ac72061dfcab6dbf077a7a111ada946e666a439f6bdd356b8eb6207ce52","compact":"96f353e3795e495ea6bfb996c40bba8bd5fa78604ec0cb22855f52b3b50c85cb","nasal":"96f353e3795e495ea6bfb996c40bba8bd5fa78604ec0cb22855f52b3b50c85cb"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-44-12","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":44,"verse":12,"english":"Even the celestials speak ill of bad name whereas fame is adored in all the regions. Therefore the high-souled exert their best to acquire reputations.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.37,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-45-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7044012","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3c2c302410d9b15991be7de39f348e6ac144c768515003de8e248d0703504b70","compact":"6e26d28360fcc08863298c4bae1aad6f58957e21b765655e850101f9bdc53486","nasal":"f20829e47580f635573ff96192b3bac57c592465c012f38812b68ea9ed5f1469"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-44-13","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":44,"verse":13,"english":"O foremost of men, what to speak of the daughter of Janaka-I can even renounce my life and yourselves in fear of a bad name.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-45-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7044013","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d706710b4dc170cbda16504111c153c9308643eb8c750e172fa0af63ddd0b958","compact":"0108ab296f16fcc3aead7b9bd95edfbcabc1ece3e598df67f500e4acb70e5b7b","nasal":"0108ab296f16fcc3aead7b9bd95edfbcabc1ece3e598df67f500e4acb70e5b7b"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-44-14","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":44,"verse":14,"english":"Do you therefore perceive into what great abyss of sorrow and ill-fame I have fallen. Up to this time I have never experienced such a mighty grief.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.857,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-45-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7044014","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d157c350ede09b1c568d8e9d8eed96d02eac7e684a35e0a45b28c4ad860aeb87","compact":"4ae09b002be009453b1f7cc6f87c11a5d8c00b17488e1c23ce5850a6ed98935d","nasal":"a3346744dff11df72c6e79a1b2defe490abe6e6fc0096455493a61f4c03064be"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-44-15","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":44,"verse":15,"english":"Do you, O Laksmana, next morning, ascending the car driven by Sumantra, take away Sītā to another country.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-45-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7044015","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6cb56a93b0ead7186a2c654d21e6d7d38ff3dd8191bccbfd45a3bf7226733d75","compact":"8a0ed5dd8e85f228183c07de1a739ea2a85be699d657ee15ce8ae57a3e8b0f02","nasal":"bd602453a6a29b93e14b7ab23bfacee1cb9f8f5cdf99277079a20c604ad4bcfa"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-44-16","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":44,"verse":16,"english":"There is a picturesque hermitage of the highsouled Vālmīki situate on the Tamasā on the other side of the river Gangā.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.857,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-45-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7044016","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"42a16d6468616cbaea6f4c9c8cda5b234baff9a71a53a7f42e4c0cb5ca8e8176","compact":"c90648f82a9043a2aa200b347680b8cd9f9dad8d49475ba9a8993b4eb1b0a202","nasal":"34e426b6727233d9fd63e5abca9f27412b27226a5143e21a2c843f38b8db1914"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-44-17","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":44,"verse":17,"english":"Do you, O delight of Raghus, soon come back, leaving behind Sitā in that lonely place. Do you carry out my words. Do yo